</style>
<h2>Asobi Review 0.2 (build 491)</h2>
<p><b>Session reels are about half the size, for the same picture.</b></p>
<ul>
<li><b>The whole-session reel is HEVC now, not H.264.</b> It was fixed at H.264 and a bitrate of width×height×8 — 16.6 Mbps at 1080p, which is why a five-minute reel came out at 581 MB. HEVC carries the same review picture at roughly half that. Measured on the same reel: 29 MB → 15 MB, with a 0.6% average difference between the two frames — the size is the only thing that changed.</li>
<li><b>New: a Format menu in the reel save dialog</b> — HEVC (recommended), H.264 for anywhere that can't play HEVC, or ProRes 422 LT for finishing. Your last choice is remembered.</li>
</ul>
]]></description>
